# The team-seat history-floor boundary ratchet (scripts/check_history_floor_boundary.sh).
#
# Per file: how many SQL literals read a floored table without the floor
# boundary (crate::history_floor). A RATCHET: counts may go down and may not
# go up, and no file may be added. Lower it with `--update`. RAISING IT IS A
# HAND EDIT, with the reason in the PR: a new member read of floored content
# must apply the floor instead.
#
# Committed at #1545 (2026-10-28). `--list` prints every counted statement.
#
# Raised by hand:
#   library_read/listing_facts.rs 1 -> 2 (#1565 follow-up): #1565 split the one
#   canonical listing CTE literal into two (LISTING_OUTCOMES_CTE). Same reads,
#   no new statement. It builds graph-wide cached facts; a floored reader never
#   reaches the cache (read_model/listing.rs admission: permission_window).
#   Adding the floor or a claim comment would change the sealed model SQL hash.
#   desktop_purge.rs 0 -> 4 -> 7 (ADR 0015, purge_desktop_data): an operator one-shot
#   that counts and selects work-session rows across a whole database to
#   delete them. Not a member read; nothing it reads is shown to a member.
#   4 -> 7 (#1594 review): the dry-run survey of blob keys, affected graphs
#   and invalidated read surfaces, read the same way for the operator.
#   ingest.rs 0 -> 1 (ADR-0016 layer 1): the ingest funnel moved here from
#   routes/ingest.rs (removed, 1). Same statement: the capture's own
#   source_versions.extraction_status, read back inside its write transaction.
unfloored backend/src/capture_admission_health.rs 5
unfloored backend/src/ingest/capture.rs 4
